    "summary": "ImageMagick: Heap Buffer Over-Write in JP2 encoder when due to incorrect handling of arguments",
    "details": "ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to version 7.1.2-26, an incorrect handling of arguments can cause a heap buffer over-write in the JP2 encoder. This issue has been fixed in version7.1.2-26.",
